  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes QAOA-in-QAOA (QAOA2), a hierarchical gate-based QAOA method for MaxCut, and reports simulator results on 2000-vertex graphs using 10 qubits with 1-layer local QAOA and 20 training iterations. On four 2000-vertex graph families, QAOA2 is generally competitive with or slightly better than Goemans-Williamson, and performance improves with larger subgraph qubit counts (8, 10, 12, 15) and better partitioning, but no practical quantum advantage is demonstrated.",
